# Trivy ignore list for the container image scan.
#
# Every entry here must be a specific, investigated CVE with a written
# justification below it — never a blanket severity/package ignore. This
# file is reviewed the same way security-policy.yaml's thresholds are:
# an entry here is a deliberate, documented risk acceptance, not a way to
# make the gate stop complaining.
#
# All entries below are the same underlying situation: gcr.io/distroless/
# nodejs22-debian12:nonroot (see app/Dockerfile) is the smallest-attack-
# -surface base image we evaluated (verified via a real local trivy scan
# across node:20-alpine, node:22-alpine, node:22-slim, and this image —
# see app/Dockerfile's comments for the actual numbers). Its libssl3 and
# libc6 packages are a few points behind Debian's own published security
# fixes; several of these CVEs have no fixed version published upstream
# at all yet (FixedVersion: null in the trivy report), so no base image
# choice would resolve them today. Distroless ships no shell and no
# package manager, so there is no way to apply an available fix ourselves
# inside this image the way `apk upgrade` or `apt-get upgrade` would on a
# fuller base — the fix has to come from distroless's own next image
# rebuild, which is upstream of this project. Re-evaluate this file (and
# drop entries that no longer apply) whenever app/Dockerfile's base image
# digest is next bumped.

